// =============================================================================
// Detection: Failed sign-in spike from a single IP (password spray / brute force)
// Lab:       Contoso Health Identity Platform
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// WHAT IT CATCHES
//   10+ CREDENTIAL failures (wrong password, locked out, expired or missing
//   password, disabled or unknown account) from ONE source IP inside any
//   10-minute window that starts on a 5-minute boundary (hopping windows:
//   :00-:10, :05-:15, :10-:20, ...; the output TimeGenerated is the window
//   start). Since 2026-11-07 (review finding D1) MFA prompts and other
//   interrupts no longer count, and a burst that straddles a clock boundary
//   is no longer split in two. Two shapes fall out of the same query:
//     - many distinct users, few attempts each  -> password spray
//     - one user, many attempts                 -> brute force / credential stuffing
//
// TABLE / SOURCE
//   SigninLogs  (Microsoft Entra ID -> Diagnostic settings -> Log Analytics).
//   Covers interactive user sign-ins. For the non-interactive flood (legacy /
//   token replay) union AADNonInteractiveUserSignInLogs — see legacy-auth.kql
//   and break-glass-signin.kql for the union pattern.
//
// LICENSE
//   - SigninLogs export to Log Analytics requires Microsoft Entra ID P1 (or P2).
//     The free tier does NOT stream sign-in logs to a workspace.
//   - Runs as a Log Analytics scheduled query or a Microsoft Sentinel rule.
//
// FALSE-POSITIVE NOTES
//   - Shared egress NAT / corporate VPN / CGNAT can concentrate many users
//     behind one IP. The hospital's own egress ranges (TrustedEgressRanges,
//     rendered by modules/monitoring from var.trusted_egress_ranges; also the
//     CA named location in production) are dropped from the brute-force
//     shape: there one user's retries are normal. The spray shape still
//     alerts from them (5+ users failing from one IP is never normal).
//   - A spray spread across many IPs never reaches 10 per IP: that is what
//     failed-signin-spray-by-asn.kql (distinct users per ASN, 1 h) is for.
//   - A looping misconfigured client (old password cached) hammers one account
//     — real, but operational not malicious; tune the single-user threshold.
//   - MFA-required codes (e.g. 50074 / 50076) and other interrupts are not
//     credential failures and are not counted (CredentialFailureCodes below).
//
// TUNABLE THRESHOLDS
//   FailureThreshold = 10 credential failures / IP / 10-minute window, windows
//   every 5 minutes (each event counts in the two windows that contain it),
//   so 10+ failures inside ANY 5 minutes always fire. One row per IP per run
//   (the window with the most failures). Both twins changed together (this
//   file and lab/splunk/detections/failed-signin-spike.spl).
//   Still a gap: 9 failures per IP per 10 minutes, forever, from one IP.
//   Smart lockout (50053) and the ASN rule are the backstop.
//
// SUGGESTED SENTINEL RULE
//   As deployed by lab/terraform/modules/monitoring: Frequency 5m · Lookback
//   1h · Trigger > 0 rows · Entities: IP=IPAddress only (UserList is a
//   dynamic array and cannot map to an Account entity). Suggested tuning
//   (not deployed): surface ErrorCodes in the incident for triage.
//
// AUTOMATED RESPONSE (Logic App - lab/monitoring/playbook-notify.json)
//   Shared by all five rules, Sentinel path only (the post-trial Log
//   Analytics alerts just email the ag-identity-secops action group).
//   Incident created -> automation rule (lab/terraform/modules/monitoring) ->
//   (1) Teams adaptive card: incident severity, title, number, created time,
//       status, description and an "Open in Sentinel" link;
//   (2) ServiceNow incident: urgency/impact from severity (Medium -> 2),
//       category "inquiry"; (3) the INC number is commented back on the
//       Sentinel incident for the audit trail.
//   NOT BUILT (production follow-up): approval-gated Graph call to add the IP
//   to a CA named location / block list.
// =============================================================================

let FailureThreshold = 10;   // credential failures from one IP in one window
let Window = 10m;            // window length
let Step = 5m;               // a new window starts every Step (hopping)
// Real credential failures only (Microsoft Entra authentication error codes):
// 50126 invalid username or password · 50053 locked (smart lockout) or
// blocked · 50055 password expired · 50056 no or invalid password on record
// · 50057 account disabled · 50034 user does not exist.
let CredentialFailureCodes = dynamic(["50126", "50053", "50055", "50056", "50057", "50034"]);
// The hospital's own egress ranges (CIDR). Empty = none trusted.
let TrustedEgressRanges = dynamic([]); // @@TRUSTED_EGRESS_RANGES@@
SigninLogs
| where TimeGenerated > ago(1h)
// ResultType is a STRING in SigninLogs.
| where ResultType in (CredentialFailureCodes)
// Each event belongs to the window that starts at its 5-minute bin and to
// the one that started 5 minutes earlier.
| extend WindowStart = pack_array(bin(TimeGenerated, Step), bin(TimeGenerated, Step) - Step)
| mv-expand WindowStart to typeof(datetime)
| summarize
      FailedCount   = count(),
      TargetedUsers = dcount(UserPrincipalName),
      UserList      = make_set(UserPrincipalName, 25),
      ErrorCodes    = make_set(ResultType, 10),
      Apps          = make_set(AppDisplayName, 10),
      Country       = any(tostring(LocationDetails.countryOrRegion)),
      FirstSeen     = min(TimeGenerated),
      LastSeen      = max(TimeGenerated)
    by IPAddress, WindowStart
| where FailedCount >= FailureThreshold
| extend Pattern = iff(TargetedUsers >= 5, "likely password spray", "likely brute force")
| extend TrustedEgress = isnotnull(parse_ipv4(IPAddress)) and ipv4_is_in_any_range(IPAddress, TrustedEgressRanges)
| where not(TrustedEgress and Pattern == "likely brute force")
// One row per IP: the window with the most failures.
| summarize arg_max(FailedCount, *) by IPAddress
| extend TimeGenerated = WindowStart
| project TimeGenerated, IPAddress, Country, FailedCount, TargetedUsers, Pattern,
          UserList, ErrorCodes, Apps, FirstSeen, LastSeen
| sort by FailedCount desc
